{"author":"did:key:z6Mkmz8SWiUshwDMszSqwzMngt7ScNmsEj7vZoFRLjpcZTm9","evaluation":{"digest":{"sha256":"89edc3ff62ce4deb12ff1c2b2467b5828cfefcaa65826a2846ad28b135921951"}},"instructions":"Return exactly ACCEPT or REJECT.","network.jinn.binary-judgment.item-sha256":"sha256:1d14100c434923ed41b01d58fb4494f5b238c663a17bc9b2294eff7973e0b831","outputs":[{"mediaType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","name":"judge-response","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.jinn.binary-judgment.observation.v1+json","name":"judge-observation","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.inspect-ai.eval-log+json","name":"inspect-log","required":false}],"payload":{"candidateAnswer":"become a sports commentator since he enjoys analyzing games and public speaking","evidence":"[D11:19 | 8:17 pm on 21 September, 2023] John: I've thought about it a lot. I want to use my platform to make a positive difference and inspire others - maybe even start a foundation and do charity work. It's important to me to make the most of the chances I get and leave a meaningful legacy.\n[D26:1 | 3:35 pm on 26 December, 2023] John: Hey Tim! Great to hear from you. My week's been busy - I started doing seminars, helping people with their sports and marketing. It's been awesome!\n[D27:26 | 5:26 pm on 2 January, 2024] John: He's a great leader and puts others first - that's why he eventually becomes king.","itemId":"urn:uuid:c7059383-1ee4-576b-8e5d-dbc789e5b56a","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:69c96bc0243eddc344014dbf2de8f90b0f2cc6370db608091d2891fac48d24eb","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What could John do after his basketball career?","referenceAnswer":"become a basketball coach since he likes giving back and leadership","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"69c96bc0243eddc344014dbf2de8f90b0f2cc6370db608091d2891fac48d24eb"}}]},"profile":{"digest":{"sha256":"ebb34d8362e2cc3135847a5ad6f3ee3d9c2d9922a2b827aa9dfcbaf440b22557"},"uri":"https://spec.jinn.network/task-profiles/binary-judgment/2.0"},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/profiles/task-execution/v1"}